    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for a high-protein dinner that beats takeout on price and macros.",
    "shop_smart":  "Canned diced green chiles give you all the roasted pepper flavor without any roasting or peeling. Stock up when they go on sale.\nA jar of salsa verde rounds out the sauce so you do not need extra spices. One jar covers the whole batch.\nPork loin keeps this cheap. It is the reason this bowl stays easy on the budget, so buy the big loin when it hits a sale.",
    "make_it":  [
                    "Set the pork loin in the slow cooker with the chopped onion, minced garlic, and chopped jalapeno.",
                    "Pour in the diced green chiles, salsa verde, green chile sauce, and chicken broth, then stir in the ground cumin, smoked paprika, cayenne, dried oregano, and a little salt and pepper.",
                    "Cover and cook on low for 7 to 8 hours until the pork shreds easily.",
                    "Shred the pork right in the pot and stir it back through the green chili sauce.",
                    "Melt the butter in a small pan, whisk in the flour to make a paste, then stir it into the chili and let it simmer a few minutes until the sauce thickens.",
                    "Squeeze in the fresh lime juice, then serve over cooked white rice and divide into containers."
                ],
